Kodis crash-loop "safe mode" is off on this box.

kodi.sh counts restarts (KODI_MAX_RESTARTS inside KODI_MAX_SECONDS) and, on a
loop, writes SAFE to .config/boot.status; kodi-safe-mode then renames
/storage/.kodi to /storage/.kodi.FAILED and reboots, so Kodi comes up on an
empty profile. That cure is worse than the disease here:

  - the rename happens AFTER symphony-userdata.service has already copied our
    guisettings.xml into /storage/.kodi/userdata, so the box loses all 31 of
    this rigs settings for that boot - including services.webserver, which
    Kodi will not start on a default profile (authentication defaults on with
    no password), leaving no JSON-RPC for the Symphony driver;
  - a transient crash loop (one bad disc, a decoder wedge) is enough to
    trigger it, and it also takes the library db, watched state and addon
    data with it;
  - the A/B slots and the relay power-cycle are the recovery path for a box
    that will not start, and neither of them destroys the profile.

kodi.sh checks only that this file exists; its contents are a comment.
